            "id": "water_application_event_behavior",
            "kind": "behavior",
            "expectation": "A layer-five water Audicle owns tide/wave/parcel/source/editor effects and continuous shader animation, including while player input is idle. Tracked presentation Entities have explicit preparation, pause/resume and close lifetimes; named computational hooks are not Audicles.",
            "procedure": "Exercise real application Configure/Step/Frame/Sample/Disturb/Edit/Pause/Close routes, disabled selection, idle animation, pause clock stability, resume attribution, errors and complete Entity/native cleanup. Verify locomotion/submergence and disturbance/editor consumers are actually wired, accepted terrain/soil revision reaches collision and reflection/refraction scene passes run on each selected graphics backend. Do not substitute helper inventory for the full connected port. WaterSystem.Edit operation source accepts a positive start tie or null, validates authored open courses, and clear-all clears selection. Authored graph/source selection save atomically on normal Close to output water-editor.json and restore at Configure; missing save uses procedural graph, malformed saves are preserved and reported. An unchanged procedural graph is not written. No parcel or natural river placement persistence is claimed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "waterpark_authored_basins",
        "description": "Install measured outdoor and grotto pool volumes and shallow flume films in native continuous water rendering. Includes four lazy-river reaches, a separate funnel catch basin and a third Sunspin funnel film course.",
        "retention": "experimental",
        "selection": "Theatre waterpark configured; Cardinal cyberworld course is shape reference only.",
        "implements": [
